  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "C.H. Robinson delivers FY2026 guidance (~$1.0bn operating income) in a still-contracting freight market, proving that most of the Lean-AI cost-out (headcount down ~31% since 2022 with volumes up) is structural. The truckload market tightens gradually rather than snapping back; NAST keeps outgrowing the Cass index but Global Forwarding stays tariff-volatile. Pre-SBC EBITDA settles near 7% of gross revenue -- above every pre-2023 year but short of a peak-cycle print -- and gross revenue grows 3-5% through the cycle. Working capital absorbs cash as revenue grows because receivables lead carrier payables.",
    "bull": "The freight cycle inflects in 2027 (truckload costs already up mid-teens YoY) and CHRW captures it with a cost base ~30% leaner than the last upcycle: AGP expands faster than headcount, operating margin prints well above the 'mid-cycle' target, and scale plus Navisphere/AI pricing widen the gap to sub-scale brokers after Convoy's exit. Tariff complexity lifts customs brokerage demand. Pre-SBC EBITDA reaches 8% of gross revenue and holds.",
    "bear": "The trough extends: new 2026 US tariffs and a USMCA review disrupt cross-border and auto freight, the Cass index keeps falling, and over-cutting headcount shows up in service quality and carrier churn. Digital freight-matching platforms and shipper-direct relationships erode take-rates, so the Lean-AI savings are passed through to customers rather than retained. Margin reverts to the pre-2023 range and revenue stalls."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "Value an asset-light freight broker on the through-cycle owner free cash flow it earns, not on a trough or peak year. Gross revenue is mostly pass-through carrier cost, so the judgment is carried by the margin on gross revenue, anchored to reaffirmed FY2026 guidance and to how much of the Lean-AI cost-out survives a cycle. SBC and the cash tax withheld on vesting awards are charged as the cost they are; buybacks keep the count flat.",
    "key_risks_to_valuation": [
      "Margin on gross revenue is the whole valuation: each 0.5pp of pre-SBC EBITDA margin is worth roughly $12-14/share in the base case.",
      "Revenue inflates with freight rates, so a rate spike can lift revenue while compressing margin %; the two paths are not independent.",
      "Working capital: a strong upcycle consumes cash (FY2021 OCF was $95M on $844M net income); the -8% capture may understate that in the bull.",
      "Equity-award withholding tax ($77M FY2025, $75M H1 2026) is elevated; if it normalises to ~$25M the SBC charge is too heavy by ~0.2-0.3pp of revenue.",
      "Terminal value carries most of the value; cap multiple 15x base vs Gordon ~17x."
    ]
  },
